Exact source floating literals in the bare-metal RV64 image.

Newlib strtof rounds through binary64, strtold writes x87 into binary128
storage, and the inherited hexadecimal path loses low digits and rounds
through binary128. Use the existing newlib integer bignums to round the
exact decimal/hexadecimal/binary rational once at its destination quantum.
No reference data or native floating intermediate is used. Public libc
conversions are unchanged; only compiler literal parsing is repaired.

Applies after 0001/0002/0003. Vendor TinyCC and frozen sum cuts stay unchanged.
See results/model/direct-float-review-2026-10-27.md and ATTRIBUTION.md.

